   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to repeal subdivision 9 of section 8-400 of the election law, in\nrelation to absentee voting in primary elections for certain party positions",
    "basePrintNo": "S9343",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9343-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Rpld §8-400 sub 9, El L",
    "lawSection": "Election Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9343\n\nSPONSOR: SEPULVEDA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to repeal subdivision 9 of section 8-400 of the election law, in\nrelation to absentee voting in primary elections for certain party posi-\ntions\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to make a conforming change to the New York\nState Election Law.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of this bill repeals § 8-400(9) of the Election Law, which\nprovides that absentee voting in primary elections shall not apply to\nthe party positions of members of the ward, town, city, or county\ncommittee.\n\nSection two of this bill establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nChapter 615 of 2019 removed language from Election Law § 7-122 that\nomitted party position of ward, town, city, or county committee from\nabsentee ballots for primary elections. Prior to 2019, such members were\nexcluded from absentee ballots due to lack of space on ballots from the\ntime that lever machines were used to cast votes. However, when such\nomission was corrected in 2019, the corresponding change was never made\nto Election Law § 8-400, which sets forth the process for absentee\nvoting. This bill would update the law in order to harmonize these\nprovisions and ensure that Election Day ballots and absentee ballots\nmatch.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
